# Agent Teams

Claude Code 2.1.246 serves `/auto go SPEC-ID --team` through its native implicit
team. Gemini does not emulate this lifecycle. On Gemini, use the platform's
normal subagent pipeline unless a Gemini-native team surface is exposed by the
runtime.

## Claude Binding

The Claude lead must verify an interactive session and
`CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1`, then launch named teammates with the
current `Agent` schema:

```python
Agent(
    description="Implement the assigned disjoint paths",
    prompt="Return exactly: owned_paths, changed_files, verification, blockers, next_required_step.",
    subagent_type="executor",
    name="builder-1",
)
```

Named teammates share the working tree and Claude's task list. Assign disjoint
file ownership, coordinate with `SendMessage`, request teammate shutdown on
completion, and rely on automatic runtime cleanup. Do not add per-call effort,
permission mode, team identity, or isolation.

`--workflow` is separate: it launches Route A with `Workflow({scriptPath,
args})`. It is never the implementation of `--team`.
